    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JOS 14:4 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For the children of Joseph were two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim. They gave no portion to the Levites in the land, except cities to dwell in, with their pasture lands for their livestock and for their property."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:4 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Joseph, Manasseh and Ephraim, took their inheritance."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:5 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "This was the border of the children of Ephraim according to their families. The border of their inheritance eastward was Ataroth Addar, to Beth Horon the upper."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:8 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "From Tappuah the border went along westward to the brook of Kanah; and ended at the sea. This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Ephraim according to their families;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 16:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "together with the cities which were set apart for the children of Ephraim in the middle of the inheritance of the children of Manasseh, all the cities with their villages."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:8 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The land of Tappuah belonged to Manasseh; but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:9 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The border went down to the brook of Kanah, southward of the brook. These cities belonged to Ephraim among the cities of Manasseh. The border of Manasseh was on the north side of the brook, and ended at the sea."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:10 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Southward it was Ephraim’s, and northward it was Manasseh’s, and the sea was his border. They reached to Asher on the north, and to Issachar on the east."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 17:17 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joshua spoke to the house of Joseph, that is, to Ephraim and to Manasseh, saying, “You are a numerous people, and have great power. You shall not have one lot only;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 20:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They set apart Kedesh in Galilee in the hill country of Naphtali, Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim, and Kiriath Arba (also called Hebron) in the hill country of Judah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:5 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The rest of the children of Kohath had ten cities by lot out of the families of the tribe of Ephraim, out of the tribe of Dan, and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:20 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The families of the children of Kohath, the Levites, even the rest of the children of Kohath, had the cities of their lot out of the tribe of Ephraim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 21:21 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They gave them Shechem with its pasture lands in the hill country of Ephraim, the city of refuge for the man slayer, and Gezer with its pasture lands,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 24:30 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathserah, which is in the hill country of Ephraim, on the north of the mountain of Gaash."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 24:33 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Eleazar the son of Aaron died. They buried him in the hill of Phinehas his son, which was given him in the hill country of Ephraim."
      }
    ],
